diff --git a/docs/decisions/002-implementation-trail.md b/docs/decisions/002-implementation-trail.md
--- a/docs/decisions/002-implementation-trail.md
+++ b/docs/decisions/002-implementation-trail.md
@@ -101,3 +101,44 @@
   calling Workers `fetch` with `Upgrade: websocket`. Workers fetch rejects
   WebSocket URL schemes before sending the handshake. Keep Bearer auth
   and the server-owned proxy; live provider transcription remains unproven.
+
+## Direct Soniox temporary-key sessions
+
+Desktop audio connects directly to Soniox. Titen authenticates the device,
+reserves its available credit up to five hours, and issues a single-use key.
+The key can start one stream within 60 seconds. Soniox enforces a fixed stream
+duration. Heartbeats cannot extend that duration. Reconnecting requires a new
+session and a new reservation.
+
+The temporary credential stays in desktop memory. The backend stores the
+provider, key expiry, and duration limit, but never the key. Finalized transcript
+segments are uploaded through authenticated heartbeat requests with stable
+sequence numbers. Existing persistence also creates Google document jobs.
+
+Client completion only marks the session finalizing. Billing uses Soniox usage
+records matched to the session reference that the backend bound to the key.
+An empty response is not proof of zero usage. Only successfully completed
+requests appear in provider logs. Unused, failed, or delayed sessions keep their
+holds until a provider record arrives or an operator investigates them.
+Definitive mint rejection releases the hold. An ambiguous timeout retains it.
+
+The stream duration cap is a wall-clock limit. It is not a guarantee that
+uploaded audio duration, model selection, or provider cost cannot exceed the
+reservation. The ledger clamps settlement to held credit. Provider spend can
+differ from Titen's accepted-audio billing, including during capture pauses.
+
+Apply the new D1 migration before enabling the desktop change. Configure
+SONIOX_API_KEY with temporary-key, transcription, and usage-log access. Configure
+TRANSCRIPTION_RECONCILE_TOKEN with a service secret. Arrange an external periodic
+POST to /api/internal/transcription-usage with that Bearer token. Account-scoped
+reconciliation also runs when fetching budget, authorizing, and ending a session.
+No scheduler
+is installed automatically. Run this endpoint after sessions end and for clients
+that crash. It rotates through up to 100 pending sessions per call, checking the least
+recently checked sessions first. Missing records remain
+reserved and require operational review. Do not deploy without reconciliation
+and monitoring for pending holds.
+
+The former audio proxy remains available only for legacy sessions. New direct
+sessions cannot connect to it. Missing Soniox configuration fails authorization
+with 503 instead of silently falling back to synthetic transcription.
